From 8cc8cd1dab2318d89c164e6961eefdd734f41126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JLab13 <jlab13@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:03:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] spi: rp2040-gpio-bridge: Use of_property_present() for i2c
 lock flag

The overlays set fast_xfer_requires_i2c_lock = <1>, so now that probe
gets that far, reading it with of_property_read_bool() warns:

  OF: /axi/pcie@1000120000/rp1/i2c@88000/spi@40: Read of boolean property 'fast_xfer_requires_i2c_lock' with a value.

Only its presence matters, so use of_property_present().

Signed-off-by: JLab13 <jlab13@icloud.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-rp2040-gpio-bridge.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-rp2040-gpio-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-rp2040-gpio-bridge.c
@@ -1035,7 +1035,7 @@ static void rp2040_gbdg_parse_dt(struct
 
 	rp2040_gbdg->fast_xfer_data_index = of_args[0].args[0];
 	rp2040_gbdg->fast_xfer_clock_index = of_args[1].args[0];
-	rp2040_gbdg->fast_xfer_requires_i2c_lock = of_property_read_bool(
+	rp2040_gbdg->fast_xfer_requires_i2c_lock = of_property_present(
 		client->dev.of_node, "fast_xfer_requires_i2c_lock");
 
 	rp2040_gbdg->gpio_base = of_iomap(dn, 0);
